{
  "key": "LAC-250",
  "url": "https://akumina.atlassian.net/browse/LAC-250",
  "summary": "LOE: Enable Resource Library search in typeahead and full search with proper linking",
  "descriptionText": "Currently, Resource Library items are not easily searchable via typeahead or clearly categorized within search results. Users need a way to quickly find and access Resource Library content directly from search.\n\nRequest:\nEnhance search functionality to include Resource Library items in both typeahead and full search results.\n\nProposed Solution:\n\n- Add a “Resource Directory” category under the Media section in typeahead search\n- Include Resource Library items in typeahead suggestions\n- Add a filter option for “Resource Directory” on the full search results page\n- Ensure all links route to the correct, functional destination (e.g., Time Entry → Workday)\n\nExpected Behavior:\n\n- Users can search for Resource Library items directly via typeahead\n- Resource items appear under a clearly labeled category (e.g., Resource Directory)\n- Users can filter to Resource Directory content on the full search results page\n- Clicking a result takes the user to the correct working destination\n\nCurrent Behavior:\n\n- Resource Library items are not easily discoverable via typeahead\n- No dedicated category or filter exists for Resource content\n- Navigation to key tools/resources is less efficient\n\nBusiness Impact:\n\n- Improves discoverability of key tools and resources\n- Reduces time spent navigating or manually locating resources\n- Enhances overall search usability and user experience\n\nPriority: Medium\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n\n- Resource Library items appear in typeahead results\n- “Resource Directory” category is available in typeahead and full search\n- Full search includes a filter for Resource Directory\n- All links correctly resolve to intended destinations\n- No regression in existing Media search functionality\n\nNote: Terry Asking client about icon to use",
  "status": "New",
  "issueType": "Task",
  "priority": "High",
  "assignee": "Diego Rosa",
